<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Muret</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1213">1213</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Muret was fought on 12 September 1213 south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>. A small crusader army under Simon de Montfort routed the much larger forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-aragon">Peter II of Aragon</a> and Raymond VI of Toulouse, killing King Peter. The defeat ended Aragonese ambitions north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> and left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> open to the crusaders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-muret.jpg" alt="Battle of Muret" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonimous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Muret.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The heaviest blows came during the Albigensian Crusade, when Simon de Montfort defeated Raymond VI and Peter II of Aragon at the <b>Battle of Muret</b> in 1213.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">County of Toulouse · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Peter II had himself crowned by Pope Innocent III in Rome in 1204, fought at the Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa in 1212 and was killed at the <b>Battle of Muret</b> in 1213, ending the Crown’s ambitions north of the Pyrenees.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…the union with Catalonia the kingdom's forces fought in the wars of the Crown of Aragon: Peter II died at the <b>Battle of Muret</b> in 1213, and James I the Conqueror led Aragonese knights in the conquests of Majorca from 1229 and of Valencia, which fell in 1238.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon · Military</a></li></ul></section>
